---
/** Company: what HLLMR Ventures is, how it operates, and a short founder note (the 2026-08 home-page bio, moved here). */
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHead from "../../components/PageHead.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, FOUNDER, LINKS, LOCALITY, OWNER } from "../../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Company · HLLMR Ventures"
  description="HLLMR Ventures LLC is a Texas company that builds software with AI agents and helps teams do the same, using the discipline of building-systems commissioning."
  sheet="Company"
>
  <PageHead
    dwg="DWG C-001 · Company"
    title="HLLMR Ventures"
    lede="A small Texas company that builds software, runs it, and helps others build with AI agents without losing track of what is true."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap co">
      <dl class="spec ident">
        <dt>Entity</dt><dd>{OWNER}, a Texas limited liability company</dd>
        <dt>Based</dt><dd>{LOCALITY}</dd>
        <dt>Founder</dt><dd>{FOUNDER}</dd>
        <dt>Contact</dt><dd><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a></dd>
        <dt>Code</dt><dd><a href={LINKS.github} rel="noopener">github.com/HLLMR</a></dd>
      </dl>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Operating principles</h2>
        <ol class="principles">
          <li><strong>Witness it.</strong> A claim that something works is checked by running it. A control that has never been seen to refuse anything is an assumption.</li>
          <li><strong>Keep the record.</strong> Decisions are written down with the options that were rejected, on the day they are made.</li>
          <li><strong>A person decides.</strong> Agents do bounded work. Merges, releases and production changes wait for a named person's approval.</li>
          <li><strong>Prove the way back.</strong> Rollback and restore are exercised before a change is approved, not discovered after it fails.</li>
          <li><strong>Own the stack.</strong> We run our own infrastructure and prefer that clients can run theirs.</li>
          <li><strong>Say the limits.</strong> Every case study ends with what it does not prove.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>From the founder</h2>
        <p>I build control systems, and lately I build software the way I was trained to build control systems.</p>
        <p>
          Twenty years in building automation and integrated building systems: the controls, physical security, fire, and
          networks that run a building, and the commissioning discipline that proves they do what the drawings say. Before
          that, the Navy's nuclear program, where you assume nothing works until you have watched it work.
        </p>
        <p>
          Now I build software with AI coding agents every day, and the same discipline turns out to be the missing piece.
          An agent will report a task complete when it is not. A control nobody has watched deny anything is an assumption.
          A plan regenerated from the code launders drift into the record. None of that is new. It is the failure mode
          every commissioning engineer already knows, arriving in an industry that has not learned to distrust a status
          point yet.
        </p>
        <p class="sig anno">{FOUNDER}, founder</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .co {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.8fr);
    gap: clamp(24px, 5vw, 72px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .ident {
    border: 1.5px solid var(--text);
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: 4px 16px;
  }
  .ident > :nth-last-child(-n + 2) {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  .ident {
    border-top: 1.5px solid var(--text);
  }
  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .principles {
    padding-left: 1.3em;
  }
  .principles li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .principles li::marker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .sig {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .co {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
